From 1695db3c56a315612bfb0e6f42e5d6a283f5a429 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 08:41:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] feat(store): vendor StoreApp.qml override +
 density-factor rendering fix
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Marathon Store app ships compiled into the marathon-shell APK
inside libstoreplugin.so as a Qt resource. mkosi.images/base/mkosi.
postinst (line 458) overrides that compiled-in copy at image-build
time by dropping this vendored StoreApp.qml at the path the manifest
references — letting us iterate on Store rendering without rebuilding
the (slow) marathon-shell APK end-to-end.

This commit captures the override delta that's been carried in the
duranium-build working tree:

* `sf` density factor — Marathon's shell chrome multiplies dimensions
  by Constants.scaleFactor (~2.0 on phone DPI), but the Store hero +
  card raw-pixel sizes weren't scaled. The visual mismatch between
  the top/bottom bars and the Store body was the original bug. Every
  fixed dimension now multiplies by `sf`.
* `railOrder` property — the Store discovery view walks
  ["mobile", "trending", "popular", "recently-added", "verified"]
  and removes apps already shown in an earlier rail, so popular apps
  don't appear in three rails on the same page.
* Comment-block cleanup at the top of the file.

This override path is itself technical debt — there are now two
sources of truth for StoreApp.qml (Marathon-Shell/apps/store/
StoreApp.qml is the compiled-in version, this one is the override).
Long-term fix is to remove the override block in mkosi.postinst and
have it pull StoreApp.qml from \$MARATHON_SHELL_SRC instead. Tracked
separately.
---
 marathon-extras/StoreApp.qml | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/marathon-extras/StoreApp.qml b/marathon-extras/StoreApp.qml
index 5b7f1b0..4d4e668 100644
--- a/marathon-extras/StoreApp.qml
+++ b/marathon-extras/StoreApp.qml
@@ -440,7 +440,7 @@ MApp {
                     tabs: [
                         { "label": "Discover",  "icon": "compass" },
                         { "label": "Installed", "icon": "package" },
-                        { "label": "Updates",   "icon": "cloud-download" }
+                        { "label": "Updates",   "icon": "cloud-arrow-down" }
                     ]
                     // refreshState() triggers the refresh-state script which
                     // rewrites installed.json + updates.json. The 1.5s
@@ -935,7 +935,7 @@ MApp {
                         anchors.leftMargin: MSpacing.md
                         anchors.rightMargin: MSpacing.md
                         spacing: MSpacing.md
-                        Icon { name: "cloud-download"; size: Constants.iconSizeMedium; color: MColors.marathonTealBright }
+                        Icon { name: "cloud-arrow-down"; size: Constants.iconSizeMedium; color: MColors.marathonTealBright }
                         ColumnLayout {
                             Layout.fillWidth: true
                             spacing: 0
@@ -1076,7 +1076,7 @@ MApp {
                 const out = [];
                 const shares = (ctx.shared || []);
                 if (shares.indexOf("network") >= 0) out.push({ icon: "wifi", label: "Network access", detail: "Sends and receives data online" });
-                if (shares.indexOf("ipc") >= 0) out.push({ icon: "share-2", label: "Inter-process communication", detail: "Talks to other apps on the device" });
+                if (shares.indexOf("ipc") >= 0) out.push({ icon: "share-network", label: "Inter-process communication", detail: "Talks to other apps on the device" });
                 const sockets = (ctx.sockets || []);
                 if (sockets.indexOf("pulseaudio") >= 0) out.push({ icon: "volume-2", label: "Audio", detail: "Play sound and record from microphones" });
                 if (sockets.indexOf("wayland") >= 0 || sockets.indexOf("fallback-x11") >= 0) out.push({ icon: "monitor", label: "Display", detail: "Draws windows on screen" });
